k192 (commit 9a9ab53) added a max_stanzas parameter to File::SOPS::Backend::Age->decrypt_data_key and ->can_decrypt, defaulting to 64, to bound age-stanza-count DoS (CVE-2026-85783). The {{$NEXT}} Changes entry says "Raise max_stanzas for a document that legitimately carries more recipients" without qualification.\n\nVerified in lib/File/SOPS.pm: there is exactly ONE call site of Backend::Age->decrypt_data_key (around line 1118, inside decrypt()), and it does NOT forward a max_stanzas argument -- it always uses the hardcoded default of 64. decrypt() itself only reads %args{encrypted,identities,format} and silently ignores any other key (no unknown-arg guard), so a caller who tries File::SOPS->decrypt(..., max_stanzas => 200) gets no error and no effect: the limit stays 64. The same applies to decrypt_file, extract, rotate and edit, which all funnel through this path. t/83-too-many-age-stanzas-are-refused.t only exercises File::SOPS::Backend::Age directly, so this gap has no test coverage at the public-API level.\n\nEffect: any real document with more than 64 age recipients is UNCONDITIONALLY unreadable through the documented public API (File::SOPS->decrypt/decrypt_file/extract/rotate/edit) -- there is no supported way to raise the limit except bypassing File::SOPS entirely and calling File::SOPS::Backend::Age plus re-implementing metadata parsing by hand. This is a functional dead end for legitimate large-recipient-list documents, and the Changes/POD text overstates what a caller can actually do.\n\nFix belongs to file-sops-api lane: either thread max_stanzas through decrypt/decrypt_file/extract/rotate/edit (%args pass-through to the one Backend::Age->decrypt_data_key call site), or correct the Changes/POD wording to state plainly that raising the limit requires calling File::SOPS::Backend::Age directly.

Maintainer-Entscheidung 2026-09-18: Option A (Durchreichung), NICHT Doku-Korrektur. max_stanzas soll ueber die oeffentliche API (decrypt/decrypt_file/extract/rotate/edit) nutzbar werden -- die Faehigkeit gab es vorher gar nicht. Default bleibt 64. An file-sops-api-Lane delegiert.

